{"id":"skills","name":"skills","aliases":[],"caption":"Create proficiency tests","authors":[{"id":"giraud","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Pierre-Amiel Giraud","year":"2020"}],"license":"lppl1.3","version":{"number":"1.0.0","date":"2020-10-21"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      This package attempts to make it easy for even a LaTeX novice\n      to prepare proficiency tests, especially in combination with\n      the <ref refid=\"exam\">exam<\u002fref> document class.\n      Thus, almost all command names are very similar.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      After defining skills in the preamble or in an external file,\n      they are declared using labels, and can optionally be set as\n      global skills. A skills table is generated to summarize the\n      evaluated competencies and to allow for writing down\n      the resulting proficiency level.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      A user’s guide attempts to explain all of the possibilities\n      in a readable way, with many examples.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/skills/README.md"},{"language":null,"details":"User guide","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/skills/skillsdoc.pdf"}],"bugs":"https://framagit.org/pagiraud/skills/-/issues","repository":"https://framagit.org/pagiraud/skills","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/skills","file":true},"miktex":"skills","texlive":"skills","topics":["exam"]}